{%- comment -%}
  Edition I teaser — replaces "category-reveal" (a Rings/Earrings/Necklaces/Bracelets catalogue
  grid) in the homepage's third slot. CAVIERA is Edition-based, not a permanent catalogue, so this
  introduces the commercial model without a product grid, fake product cards, or a link to
  /collections/all. Informational by design while Edition I has no dedicated page yet — cta_text/
  cta_url are both blank by default; the teaser reads as complete with no action at all.

  Images ("Edition media 01/02/03" in the Theme Editor — edition_image_1/2/3 as settings IDs,
  unchanged, to preserve any values already saved): media 01 is the primary/larger image, falling
  back to the same bundled default the hero uses (assets/15_oryx_necklace_on_model.png, the only
  jewellery/object photograph bundled with this theme) when unset. media 02/03 are each either a
  merchant's own dedicated image OR — per the visual-tuning brief's explicit guidance — a distinct
  crop/scale/object-position treatment of THAT SAME base photo when left blank, so the Aerra
  sequence below always has three genuinely different-looking visual states even with only one real
  asset available. [data-derived="true"] on media-secondary/media-detail marks exactly this
  reused-photo case for caviera-home.css's distinct crop rules; a merchant's own dedicated image
  never gets that attribute and renders as itself, uncropped-by-code.

  Aerra-style sticky progression (min-width: 900px only — see caviera-home.css): the section is a
  [data-caviera-pin] tall wrapper (assets/caviera-scroll-progress.js writes --caviera-progress onto
  it, 0 at entry/1 at exit); .caviera-edition-teaser__inner holds at the top of the viewport for
  that whole distance via position: sticky. Media 01 tightens into a closer crop, media 02 rises in
  over it, media 03 arrives last as a small detail inset, then the section releases directly into
  Object in focus. Below 900px (and whenever the script is skipped/blocked/under reduced motion)
  every image simply renders at its resting, fully visible state — see the var(--caviera-progress,
  0) fallback on each consumer in caviera-home.css. Pin height is deliberately modest (see the
  [data-caviera-pin] media query in caviera-home.css) — just enough scroll room for the crop/
  crossfade sequence to read, not a long dead hold once it's finished.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign img1 = section.settings.edition_image_1
  assign img2 = section.settings.edition_image_2
  assign img3 = section.settings.edition_image_3
  assign bundled_file = '15_oryx_necklace_on_model.png'
  assign use_bundled = false
  if img1 == blank
    assign use_bundled = true
  endif
  assign has_meta = false
  if section.settings.edition_number != blank or section.settings.edition_status != blank
    assign has_meta = true
  endif
  assign edition_num = section.settings.edition_number | default: '01'
  assign token_text = 'No. ' | append: edition_num

  # media 02/03: a merchant's own dedicated image always wins; otherwise both reuse media 01 (or
  # the bundled default) so there are always three visual states, never a state that simply never
  # renders. use_bundled_2/3 tracks which of the three code paths (dedicated Shopify image object,
  # dedicated-but-reusing-the-bundled-file, or reusing img1 itself) so width/height/src resolve
  # correctly either way.
  assign img2_derived = false
  assign img2_render = img2
  if img2 == blank
    assign img2_derived = true
    assign img2_render = img1
  endif
  assign img3_derived = false
  assign img3_render = img3
  if img3 == blank
    assign img3_derived = true
    assign img3_render = img1
  endif
-%}
<section id="edition-i" class="caviera-section caviera-edition-teaser" data-scheme="{{ section.settings.color_scheme | default: 'obsidian' }}" data-caviera-pin>
  <div class="container caviera-edition-teaser__inner">
    <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__copy" data-reveal>
      {%- if has_meta -%}
        <span class="caviera-edition-teaser__meta label" aria-hidden="true">
          {{- section.settings.edition_number -}}
          {%- if section.settings.edition_number != blank and section.settings.edition_status != blank %} / {% endif -%}
          {{- section.settings.edition_status -}}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Drkst-style typographic moment: this heading (nested [data-reveal] of its own, independent
          of the copy block's outer reveal above) enters oversized and settles — see [data-reveal-
          style="drkst"] in caviera-motion.css — AND, being inside the [data-caviera-pin] wrapper
          above, continues drifting a further few vw horizontally in step with --caviera-progress
          for as long as the section stays pinned (see .caviera-edition-teaser__heading.is-visible in
          caviera-motion.css) — a visible, continuous, architectural movement rather than a single
          one-shot entrance. Opt-out via heading_motion below; the plain static heading renders with
          no code change either way.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <h2
          class="caviera-edition-teaser__heading"
          {%- if section.settings.heading_motion %} data-reveal data-reveal-style="drkst"{% endif %}
        >
          {{ section.settings.heading }}
          {%- if section.settings.year_label != blank -%}
            <span class="caviera-edition-teaser__year">{{ section.settings.year_label }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </h2>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
        <p class="body-text caviera-edition-teaser__body">{{ section.settings.body }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.cta_text != blank and section.settings.cta_url != blank -%}
        <a href="{{ section.settings.cta_url }}" class="link-underline caviera-edition-teaser__cta">{{ section.settings.cta_text }}</a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__media"{% if section.settings.show_token %} data-caviera-drag-zone{% endif %}>
      <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__media-primary" data-reveal data-reveal-style="crop">
        {%- if img1 != blank -%}
          <img
            src="{{ img1 | image_url: width: 1000 }}"
            srcset="{{ img1 | image_url: width: 600 }} 600w, {{ img1 | image_url: width: 1000 }} 1000w, {{ img1 | image_url: width: 1400 }} 1400w"
            sizes="(min-width: 900px) 42vw, 84vw"
            width="{{ img1.width }}"
            height="{{ img1.height }}"
            alt="{{ img1.alt | default: '' | escape }}"
            loading="lazy"
          >
        {%- elsif use_bundled -%}
          <img
            src="{{ bundled_file | asset_url }}"
            width="521" height="358"
            alt=""
            loading="lazy"
          >
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        STATE 02 — always renders now (previously only when a dedicated media 02 was set): a real
        merchant image if provided, otherwise media 01/the bundled default reused with a distinct
        "closer jewellery crop" (see [data-derived="true"] in caviera-home.css) so there is always a
        genuine second visual state to crossfade into, never a state that just never appears.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__media-secondary" data-derived="{{ img2_derived }}" data-reveal data-reveal-style="mask" style="transition-delay: 140ms;">
        {%- if img2_render != blank -%}
          <img
            src="{{ img2_render | image_url: width: 700 }}"
            srcset="{{ img2_render | image_url: width: 400 }} 400w, {{ img2_render | image_url: width: 700 }} 700w, {{ img2_render | image_url: width: 1000 }} 1000w"
            sizes="(min-width: 900px) 24vw, 56vw"
            width="{{ img2_render.width }}"
            height="{{ img2_render.height }}"
            alt="{{ img2_render.alt | default: '' | escape }}"
            loading="lazy"
          >
        {%- elsif use_bundled -%}
          {%- comment -%} img2 derived from the bundled default too (img1 also blank). {%- endcomment -%}
          <img src="{{ bundled_file | asset_url }}" width="521" height="358" alt="" loading="lazy">
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        STATE 03 — same always-renders principle as media 02 above: a real merchant detail image if
        provided, otherwise the base image reused a third time with a tighter, differently-centred
        "abstract/detail" crop (see [data-derived="true"] in caviera-home.css) rather than never
        appearing. Only ever a small inset, arriving last in the scroll sequence at 900px+.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__media-detail" data-derived="{{ img3_derived }}">
        {%- if img3_render != blank -%}
          <img
            src="{{ img3_render | image_url: width: 500 }}"
            srcset="{{ img3_render | image_url: width: 300 }} 300w, {{ img3_render | image_url: width: 500 }} 500w, {{ img3_render | image_url: width: 700 }} 700w"
            sizes="(min-width: 900px) 16vw, 40vw"
            width="{{ img3_render.width }}"
            height="{{ img3_render.height }}"
            alt="{{ img3_render.alt | default: '' | escape }}"
            loading="lazy"
          >
        {%- elsif use_bundled -%}
          <img src="{{ bundled_file | asset_url }}" width="521" height="358" alt="" loading="lazy">
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Bureau Nine's Edition/spatial-progression idea, translated via the same Toasted-Buns
        draggable-artifact system as the hero's House Seal — a small, bounded Edition plaque token
        (rendered as a rectangular archival plaque — see .caviera-drag-token--number in caviera-
        home.css — not the more decorative circular medallion), floating over the primary image
        rather than fixed to one point. Desktop pointer only; fully visible and static everywhere
        else, per assets/caviera-drag-token.js.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.show_token -%}
        {%- render 'caviera-drag-token', type: 'number', text: token_text, mode: 'dark', cue: 'Move' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Edition I teaser",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "Colour", "default": "obsidian",
      "options": [
        { "value": "obsidian", "label": "Obsidian" },
        { "value": "cinnabar", "label": "Cinnabar" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Content" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "edition_number", "label": "Number", "default": "01" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "edition_status", "label": "Status", "default": "Upcoming", "info": "Quiet metadata, not a sale badge — avoid hype language (\"Limited drop\", \"Only X left\", \"Coming soon!!!\")." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "EDITION I" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "heading_motion", "label": "Architectural heading movement", "default": true, "info": "The heading enters slightly oversized and settles, then continues drifting a few vw horizontally while the section stays pinned. Off falls back to the plain static heading with no motion at all." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "year_label", "label": "Year", "default": "2026" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Supporting line", "default": "The first CAVIERA Edition is in preparation." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_text", "label": "Action text (optional)", "info": "Leave blank to keep the teaser purely informational — appropriate while Edition I has no dedicated page yet. Avoid \"Add to Bag\"/\"Shop Edition\"/\"Buy Now\"." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "cta_url", "label": "Action link (optional)", "info": "Only shown when Action text above is also set. Never point this at /collections/all." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Images" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Three visual states in the scroll sequence. Any left blank temporarily reuse Edition media 01 (or the bundled default) with a distinct crop, rather than never appearing — replace with real Edition campaign photography here at any time, no code change required." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "edition_image_1", "label": "Edition media 01 (primary)", "info": "Gender-neutral jewellery/object imagery preferred — this House is for both men and women. Falls back to a bundled default when left blank." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "edition_image_2", "label": "Edition media 02 (optional)", "info": "A closer/secondary state. Falls back to a cropped treatment of media 01 when left blank." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "edition_image_3", "label": "Edition media 03 (optional)", "info": "A small detail inset, arriving last. Falls back to a differently cropped treatment of media 01 when left blank." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Interaction" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_token", "label": "Show draggable Edition plaque token", "default": true, "info": "A small, bounded, draggable Edition-number token floating over the primary image — desktop pointer input only. Stays static and fully visible on touch, keyboard-only, and reduced-motion visits." }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Edition I teaser" }],
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["index"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
